WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:01.149
Speaker 1: All right.

00:00:01.149 --> 00:00:06.910
Let's hit a couple of other things here as
we continue with today's show, we continue

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:12.460
to wonder about what the 2024 presidential
election is going to look like.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:15.809
And a big part of that is is Joe Biden going
to run for reelection?

00:00:15.809 --> 00:00:17.150
We don't have an answer to that question.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:21.320
Yet another part of it is is Donald Trump
going to run for the Republican primary?

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:23.060
And we don't have an answer to that yet, either.

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:27.949
There is a new poll out which says that as
of right now, that's basically a dead heat

00:00:27.949 --> 00:00:29.769
race Biden versus Trump.

00:00:29.769 --> 00:00:37.160
If that were to be it, I believe it was about
45 for each a tie, statistically a tie within

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:38.180
the margin of error.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:44.010
And we can, of course, raise questions about
how valuable is a poll.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:52.040
I guess we are two years and nine months,
so 24, 33 months from that election.

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:56.261
It's probably not particularly valuable other
than to tell us that as of right now, there

00:00:56.261 --> 00:01:01.310
is still great appetite from tens of millions
of people in this country for Donald Trump

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:02.420
to be president again.

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:09.490
As I've said before, I believe that a big
factor in whether Trump will or won't run

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:13.170
again is Trump's health in 2023 and 2024.

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:15.220
He's not a particularly healthy guy.

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:17.850
He's not a particularly young guy.

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:23.890
And it's a statistical reality that his health
in 2024 may not lend itself to a presidential

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:24.890
campaign.

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:26.140
I don't know, and I'm not wishing him harm.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:30.290
I'm just saying it's aside from the will he
believe he can win.

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:32.610
Will he be distracted with something else?

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:36.810
Whatever the health issue is, is a real question,
and I'm not saying it's not a real question

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:39.119
for Joe Biden, either.

00:01:39.119 --> 00:01:43.800
That being said, we are starting to see signs
of interest from Donald Trump in running in

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:44.920
2024.

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:49.930
One of those signs of interest is that almost
at the turn of the new year, Trump has already

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:53.810
restarted rallies, doing a rally in Florence,
Arizona, on January 15th.

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:58.760
He'll be doing a rally in Conroe, Texas, where
we will have a correspondent, by the way,

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:00.720
this Saturday, January 29.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:04.810
So he seems very interested in being involved
in continuing to be sort of a kingmaker in

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:09.130
the context of the midterms in order to then
justify running in 2024.

00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:15.799
Here's another just little hint this is Donald
Trump golfing, which he does a lot now, and

00:02:15.799 --> 00:02:21.959
some kind of sycophant who's filming him teeing
off refers to him as the 45th president of

00:02:21.959 --> 00:02:27.269
the United States and then Donald Trump, says
the 45th and the 47th.

00:02:27.269 --> 00:02:31.549
Just another little sign that indeed, he may
be planning on running.

00:02:31.549 --> 00:02:33.409
Take a look.

00:02:33.409 --> 00:02:37.760
Speaker 3: Oh, you're so lucky to likely to
be

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:39.260
Speaker 5: one of those lucky.

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:47.629
We'll be lucky if we're up first on TV.

00:02:47.629 --> 00:02:53.549
46th President of the United States, 45th
and 47th first.

00:02:53.549 --> 00:02:55.420
Yes, I love Mr. Trump.

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:59.569
Speaker 3: Oh gentlemen,
Speaker 1: I'm sure everybody tells him how

00:02:59.569 --> 00:03:01.040
great his tee shot is, right?

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:02.379
No matter how good it is.

00:03:02.379 --> 00:03:05.629
Speaker 5: Say you're beautiful.

00:03:05.629 --> 00:03:06.939
Easy game.

00:03:06.939 --> 00:03:12.389
I think it's pretty boring to be middle all
the time.

00:03:12.389 --> 00:03:14.549
You want to keep it low when shrunk.

00:03:14.549 --> 00:03:15.780
Speaker 1: Yes, exactly.

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:16.780
All right.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:21.879
So, you know, I don't know how much we need
to or should read into that.

00:03:21.879 --> 00:03:27.930
But needless to say, it's just another little
sign, another small indicator that indeed,

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:31.290
Donald Trump may, may be planning to run in
2024.

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:35.180
And the scariest part is, as of right now,
if the election were held today, he might

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:36.040
actually win

